.TH WEIGH 1 "September 2026" "weigh 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
weigh \- obtain typed judgments and native probabilities
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B weigh \-m openrouter/MODEL
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B weigh help
.br
.B weigh version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Weigh reads one versioned JSON request from standard input through EOF,
makes one native OpenRouter Decisions request, validates the entire response,
and writes one JSON result followed by a newline to standard output.
Diagnostics use standard error. Weigh applies no thresholds or actions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-m " MODEL"
Required explicit model with the prefix openrouter/.
The remaining name is sent verbatim, including an initial tilde.
For example, openrouter/~typesafe/jev-latest.
.TP
.BI \-timeout " DURATION"
Positive duration covering input, authorization reads, and inference.
Default 30s. SIGINT and SIGTERM cancel outstanding work and return status 1.
.TP
.BI \-endpoint " URL"
Full endpoint URL. Default https://openrouter.ai/api/alpha/decisions.
HTTPS is required; HTTP is allowed only for literal loopback IP addresses.
URL credentials, queries, and fragments are refused. Redirects are refused.
.TP
.BI \-header-fd " N"
Read one Authorization header through EOF from descriptor N, at least 3.
The header is bounded at 8192 bytes; a final LF or CRLF is allowed.
This selection takes precedence over OPENROUTER_API_KEY without fallback.
.SH INPUT
Exactly one object with fields version, state, and questions.
Version must be the integer 1. State must be a JSON string, object, or array.
Nested numeric literals retain precision. Questions is a nonempty object of
named questions. IDs are at most 256 UTF-8 bytes, nonempty, without controls.
.TP
.B choice
Fields: type (choice), question (description), options (an object mapping
2 to 255 option IDs to descriptions). Null descriptions use the option name alone.
.TP
.B score
Fields: type (score), question (description), levels (an ordered array of
2 to 10 descriptions). Positions start at zero.
.TP
.B probability
Fields: type (probability), question (proposition or question description).
Optional criteria must contain exactly true and false descriptions.
.PP
A description is nonempty text, a JSON object, or an array. Null is allowed
only as a choice option description. Structured fields are forwarded as data;
Weigh assigns no meaning to their keys. Numeric literals retain precision.
.PP
Question IDs identify answers; meanings belong in the descriptions.
All questions share state but do not consume one another's answers.
The provider mapping uses instructions for question, criteria for options or
levels, preserves probability criteria, and uses noul for probability.
Unknown fields, duplicate decoded keys,
invalid UTF-8 or unmatched surrogate escapes, and trailing documents fail.
.SH OUTPUT
Fields: version (1), model (requested and reported names), answers, and
optional metadata. Each answer has type and value. Choice values are option
IDs; score values are fractional positions; probability values are in [0,1].
Choice and score answers include complete native probabilities objects.
Score distribution keys are zero-based level indices written as strings.
.PP
Probabilities must be finite, in [0,1], cover exactly the requested support,
and have positive total reported mass. For observed hundredth rounding,
exact multiples of 0.01 get interpretation intervals of plus or minus 0.005,
clipped to the allowed range. More precise values get no rounding allowance.
Probability intervals must permit a normalized distribution. A score must
be in range and its interval must intersect that distribution's possible
weighted means. Comparisons use 1e-6 absolute numerical slack.
This is an empirical compatibility policy, not a provider precision guarantee;
all native numbers are preserved without rounding or renormalization.
A supplied score legend must match the requested levels, ignoring object order
and string escape spelling but requiring array order and numeric literal spelling.
Missing distributions fail; they are never filled, normalized, or invented.
.PP
Optional metadata preserves service-reported request_id, provider, usage
(input_tokens, output_tokens, optional cost), and confidence by question ID.
Unknown native response fields fail explicitly. Missing metadata stays absent.
Jev confidence summarizes distribution concentration, not measured correctness
or the likelihood that a proposed change will improve future work.
The reported model name does not establish immutable model weights.
.SH LIMITS
Input, encoded native request and response: 8 MiB each.
Native encoding is bounded before credential reads or networking.
JSON nesting: 64 containers.
Questions: 1024. IDs: 256 UTF-8 bytes. Authorization header: 8192 bytes.
Response headers: 64 KiB. Excess data is refused, not truncated.
These local limits do not replace provider token limits; no token estimation
or automatic truncation is performed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPENROUTER_API_KEY
Bearer credential, unless an authorization descriptor is explicitly selected.
No credential acquisition, storage, or refresh is performed.
.PP
Standard Go HTTP proxy environment behavior applies to the transport.
No configuration file, default model, or session directory is read.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
One valid inference, including negative or uncertain judgments.
This does not mean a candidate passed a task-specific check.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime, credential, service, protocol, timeout, cancellation, or output error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid invocation or locally invalid request. No inference was attempted.
.SH COMPOSITION
Record may capture the input, output, diagnostics, and exit status externally.
Its replay makes no model call. Callers own thresholds, fallback, retries,
acceptance, and actions. A Ply checker must map Weigh failures to its own
broken-check status, not pass exit 1 through as ordinary candidate rejection.
.PP
Ask atomic semantic questions together. Filter irrelevant state and compute
counts, dates and arithmetic in caller code. Include a none-of-the-above option
when appropriate; a choice compares only its supplied alternatives.
Use probability for whether a proposition holds and score for degree.
Evaluate downstream improvements separately before promoting them.
.PP
All response validation precedes output. A write error may leave partial bytes;
consumers must check status. Error bodies and private input are not printed.
At most one inference request is made; redirects and retries are disabled.
A timeout does not prove that no work or billing occurred at the service.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
The backend uses OpenRouter's alpha Decisions protocol, not Chat Completions.
Offline fixtures verify protocol and process behavior. Live compatibility and
judgment accuracy require a separate explicitly selected evaluation.
The backend schema permits omitted distributions; Weigh deliberately refuses
such responses instead of silently weakening its public contract.
